    "title": "LESSON 25: EVERYDAY GREEK III",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "These twenty were not built from parts.",
          "English took each one whole, as it stood",
          "in Greek, and kept everything but the",
          "ending.",
          "",
          "  zone      ζώνη        a belt",
          "  arctic    ἄρκτος      bear",
          "  climate   κλίμα       a slope",
          "  magnet    μαγνῆτις    of Magnesia",
          "",
          "The north is named for the Great Bear that",
          "wheels overhead, and a klima was the tilt",
          "of the earth toward the sun, so each band",
          "of latitude was one.",
          "",
          "One impostor: nebula is Latin for mist.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 20 CARDS: Greek taken whole."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 25"
      }
    ]
